{"title": "Amit Shah offers Parliament debate; Rahul Gandhi demands accountability for student crackdown", "summary": "Union Home Minister Amit Shah stated he was ready for a debate in Parliament and to answer all opposition questions, even suggesting the session could extend late into the night. Congress leader Rahul Gandhi rejected Shah's debate offer, demanding accountability for an alleged crackdown on students during protests. Gandhi also claimed Modi's image was destroyed and that the Prime Minister and Shah must face consequences. The opposition also raised concerns about the FCRA Bill, calling it anti-minority, while the government defended it, stating foreign funds cannot flow without law. The FCRA Bill was sent to a Joint Parliamentary Committee.", "summary_points": ["Union Home Minister Amit Shah expressed readiness for a debate in Parliament and to answer opposition questions.", "Amit Shah suggested the Parliament session could continue late into the night.", "Rahul Gandhi rejected Shah's debate offer and demanded accountability for an alleged student crackdown.", "Rahul Gandhi stated that the Prime Minister and Amit Shah must face consequences.", "Opposition members called the FCRA Bill anti-minority, while the government defended it as necessary for controlling foreign funds.", "The FCRA Bill was sent to a Joint Parliamentary Committee."], "title_hi": "अमित शाह ने संसद में बहस की पेशकश की; राहुल गांधी ने छात्र कार्रवाई पर जवाबदेही मांगी", "summary_hi": "केंद्रीय गृह मंत्री अमित शाह ने कहा कि वह संसद में बहस के लिए और विपक्ष के सभी सवालों के जवाब देने के लिए तैयार हैं, यहां तक कि उन्होंने सुझाव दिया कि सत्र देर रात तक चल सकता है। कांग्रेस नेता राहुल गांधी ने शाह के बहस के प्रस्ताव को खारिज कर दिया और छात्रों पर कथित कार्रवाई के लिए जवाबदेही की मांग की। गांधी ने यह भी दावा किया कि मोदी की छवि नष्ट हो गई है और प्रधानमंत्री और शाह को इसके परिणाम भुगतने होंगे। विपक्ष ने FCRA विधेयक को अल्पसंख्यक विरोधी बताते हुए चिंता जताई, जबकि सरकार ने इसका बचाव करते हुए 